-d49cebd4-4997-4622-9c4a-26f71f907ac8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"84259c3e12a9b305a8a38ff5a5ce1066660df3ced141f2e98ee1e499e0a222a4","event_uuid":"7b3ac0ce-e8d9-482e-8e7a-06457ede489c","position":{"commit_sha":"8073981485d42ab0201206d4f78cf4528f7c3a6b","position":"1787505845477901001-7b3ac0ce-e8d9-482e-8e7a-06457ede489c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"828301d810ddbf38d58e8086db063dbe7b2a46a7820e2a778c56f0f43b26df5b","event_uuid":"6c4c9928-9bd9-4108-b2d9-656a3babf865","position":{"commit_sha":"165597f8e25f631e13fe310fc17c4d953740e61d","position":"1787513137414223001-6c4c9928-9bd9-4108-b2d9-656a3babf865"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e4adbff3a4f9c7c6d4f73b87d7ef299fbb797c7a165aa4efd2ab85e2fc5d360a","event_uuid":"3b064339-155a-4f8b-9e51-4fd3607271c8","position":{"commit_sha":"966b36f38d18e06a7286d8807ab3f5d18b5fdaae","position":"1787513459651838001-3b064339-155a-4f8b-9e51-4fd3607271c8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"DESIGN DECISION (operator-ratified 2026-08-22): implement the reconciler outbound-comment invariant check — every successfully posted Jira comment must have its returned comment ID recorded locally; divergence (post succeeded, local comment_ids unchanged) raises a bridge alert. Alert firing is DEBOUNCED ACROSS 2 CONSECUTIVE RECONCILE PASSES: it fires only when the same divergence is observed in 2 consecutive passes, matching the N-of-M alarm philosophy of the voter-observability lane. NOT per-pass immediate firing. This adjudicates the first acceptance criterion (per-pass vs debounced): debounced, N=2 consecutive.","timestamp":1787437790929575001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation landed for review: Gerrit change 2135 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2135), commit 7752130f5d9b. Plan review PASSED + signed; claim taken. RED-first tests (15 new, all green after implementation): single divergent pass silent / 2 consecutive fire / healthy pass resets / idle healthy / 3rd pass deduped / corrupt state fails open / legacy store no-op / posted-counter seam counts a post whose recording no-ops. Gates: make lint rc=0, mypy clean (638 files), complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0, module-size contract green (reconcile.py exactly 800 after moving _write_prev_snapshot_key_set to reconcile_helpers), 442 targeted reconciler tests pass. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1787444735501692001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787397425216542001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dbf523c9-2359-47d1-a2ac-6d4b16f580d3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2399-5e49-6b28-4d59"},{"link_uuid":"d49cebd4-4997-4622-9c4a-26f71f907ac8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d3a0-eaee-e2bc-46c8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFiled from the escape analysis on marshy-chummy-coot (2399-5e49-6b28-4d59). The silently-inert primary dedup guard (bug aa7b, origin 789c) left an invariant violation visible in committed production state for the feature's entire life: `.bridge_state/bindings.json` showed `comment_ids == 0` while bindings grew past 2,475 and outbound comment posts kept succeeding. No layer read that signal. This ticket adds the layer that reads it.\n\nDESIGN DECISION (operator-ratified 2026-08-22, recorded as a ticket comment): every successfully posted outbound Jira comment must have its returned comment ID recorded locally; divergence (post succeeded, local `comment_ids` unchanged) raises a bridge alert. Alert firing is DEBOUNCED ACROSS 2 CONSECUTIVE RECONCILE PASSES — it fires only when the same divergence is observed in 2 consecutive passes, matching the N-of-M alarm philosophy of the voter-observability lane. Not per-pass immediate firing. This adjudicates the first original acceptance criterion.\n\n## Approach\nIn-process, operation-linked (no CI trigger — runs wherever the reconciler runs, satisfying `project.portability` by construction), reusing seams that already exist:\n\n1. **Count successful posts at the shared enactment seam.** Both outbound comment enactment sites — `create_one` (dispatch_one.py:389-393) and `_update_one_dispatch_comments` (dispatch_apply_phases.py:386-390) — already call the shared `_record_comment_id(binding_store, entry, result)` (dispatch_apply_phases.py:311) immediately after a successful `add_comment` return. Add a guarded `note_comment_posted()` call there BEFORE its recording guards, so every successful post is tallied even when recording no-ops (the exact failure class this invariant watches).\n2. **Counters live on the `BindingStore` facade** (binding_store.py:121): per-pass posted counter (`note_comment_posted` / `comment_posts_this_pass`), `comment_ids_count()` (len of the `comment_ids` map owned by `BindingLifecycle.record_comment_id`, binding_lifecycle.py:484), and a baseline `comment_ids` count captured at construction. The store is constructed once per pass in `_load_snapshots`, so \"gained this pass\" = count now − count at load.\n3. **Pure debounce step in `invariants.py`** (the established invariants home, cf. `detect_at_most_one_local_id`): `step_comment_divergence(prev_consecutive, divergent) -> (new_consecutive, fire)` — a healthy observation (no posts, or posts with map growth) resets the counter to 0; a divergent observation increments it; fire only when the count reaches 2. Directly unit-testable, no I/O.\n4. **IO check `check_comment_id_recording(binding_store, repo_root, pass_id)` in `invariants.py`**: reads posted/gained off the store, loads the cross-pass counter from `bridge_state/comment_id_divergence.json` (local scratch, same residency as `bridge_state/bridge_alerts`; corrupt/absent state fails open to 0), runs the pure step, persists the new state, and on fire appends a record through the existing sibling `alert_store` (`append`/`is_deduped`, 24h dedup key `bridge-alert:comment-id-divergence`) whose message names the invariant and the pass.\n5. **End-of-pass hook**: one fail-open `try/except` call to `ctx.invariants_mod.check_comment_id_recording(...)` inside `_persist_and_log`'s persist branch (reconcile.py:613; `ctx.invariants_mod` is already loaded at reconcile.py:250). Runs once per pass, after the binding-store save, skipped in no-write mode.\n\nreconcile.py is at 799 LOC against the 800 hard cap, so `_write_prev_snapshot_key_set` (reconcile.py:607, no references outside reconcile.py) moves to `reconcile_helpers.py` along the existing re-export seam (reconcile.py:59-63 already loads `_helpers` and re-binds names), keeping the module under the cap.\n\nRiskiest assumption: both enactment sites reach `_record_comment_id` on every successful post — confirmed by reading dispatch_one.py:389-393 and dispatch_apply_phases.py:386-390 (the call is unconditional on the success path); the RED test for scenario (b) exercises the counting seam first, before the debounce plumbing is built on it.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py` — posted counter + `comment_ids_count()` + at-load baseline on the facade\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py` — count the post in `_record_comment_id` before the recording guards\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/invariants.py` — pure debounce step + `check_comment_id_recording` (state file + alert append)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py` — fail-open end-of-pass call in `_persist_and_log`; move `_write_prev_snapshot_key_set` out\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py` — receives `_write_prev_snapshot_key_set`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_comment_id_divergence_invariant.py` — new (RED-first)\n\n## Testing\nRED-first hermetic unit tests over a tmp tracker dir (no Jira, no network; the `spec_from_file_location` loader convention of test_binding_store_comment_ids.py):\n- (a) divergence observed once (posted>0, comment_ids gained none) → counter=1, NO alert record in `bridge_state/bridge_alerts/*.jsonl`\n- (b) same divergence in 2 consecutive passes → alert record present; its message names the invariant and the pass_id\n- (c) divergence in pass 1, healthy pass 2 (recording works), divergence in pass 3 → counter reset between, NO alert\n- healthy pass (posts recorded) and idle pass (no posts) → no alert, counter stays 0\n- pure-step table test for `step_comment_divergence`\n- `_record_comment_id` counts a successful post even when the entry carries no `local_comment_key` (recording no-ops, the post still tallies)\n- corrupt state file → fails open to counter 0, pass does not raise\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The pure debounce step fires only on the 2nd consecutive divergent observation and a healthy observation resets the counter; checked by the pure-step unit test passing\n- [x] Every successful outbound comment post is tallied at the shared `_record_comment_id` seam independent of whether recording succeeds; checked by the no-`local_comment_key` unit test passing\n- [x] A divergent pass followed by a second divergent pass appends a `bridge_alerts` JSONL record (deduped via `alert_store.is_deduped`) whose message names the invariant and the pass; checked by scenario-(b) unit test asserting the record's key, pass_id and message\n- [x] One divergent pass alone, and a divergence resolved between passes, produce NO alert; checked by scenario-(a)/(c) unit tests passing\n- [x] Cross-pass debounce state lives in `bridge_state/comment_id_divergence.json` and a corrupt/absent file fails open to 0 without breaking the pass; checked by the corrupt-state unit test passing\n- [x] `make lint` (ruff + format + complexity ratchet `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`), `make typecheck`, and the targeted reconciler test selection pass; every `src/rebar` file stays ≤800 LOC (module-size gate); checked by the commands exiting 0 in-session\n\n## Non-goals\nNo new review criterion, no CI-coupled trigger (ci-gate-compat is rejected precedent), no change to the dedup guard itself (fixed in 8d98c298fa8), no bug auto-filing from this alert (the at-most-one invariant's filing sink is not extended to it).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"posted counter + comment_ids_count + at-load baseline on the facade"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py","reason":"count the successful post in _record_comment_id before the recording guards"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/invariants.py","reason":"pure debounce step + check_comment_id_recording (state file + alert append)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"fail-open end-of-pass invariant call; move _write_prev_snapshot_key_set out to stay under the 800 LOC cap"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"receives _write_prev_snapshot_key_set"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_comment_id_divergence_invariant.py","reason":"new RED-first hermetic unit tests for the debounced invariant"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","d3a0-eaee-e2bc-46c8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6c4c9928-9bd9-4108-b2d9-656a3babf865","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0fa2-fdcb-229e-41a0","ticket_type":"task","title":"Reconciler pass invariant: comment posts succeeded but comment_ids gained none","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e6feb61a-2218-4a1c-8528-ed9f97a282a5","74e4aa84-233a-4307-b2c2-4c5b5d402bf9","7918fd56-19f2-4492-bf68-b965a269b418","143d463c-e6f6-4215-8d37-0d4ee2a1f892","135e63b6-f8f6-4f70-ab9d-49688b455902","2ca12d41-1dcd-4856-9bc4-7369fdd93c23","e9c2d656-fb5d-431c-9a55-4e57a514fc16","d49cebd4-4997-4622-9c4a-26f71f907ac8","7b3ac0ce-e8d9-482e-8e7a-06457ede489c","6c4c9928-9bd9-4108-b2d9-656a3babf865","3b064339-155a-4f8b-9e51-4fd3607271c8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787519388924851001,"uuid":"be00e5be-113c-4cbe-8b0d-9f344edfc9df"}